# Kira language surface

Facts that trip up new writers.

## Syntax facts

- Declarations initialize with braces: `name: Type { value }`, a struct `name: Pt { x = 1, y = 2 }` or `{ 1, 2 }`
  (a lone value is the value itself); `=` only names a field or an argument, or changes a `Mutable`.
  The old `name: Type = expr` is refused; `kira --fix-decl-equals FILE...` rewrites it. A value of function type
  is written `f: Fx<T1<Int32>, Int32> { g }`.
- Ranges: `a..b` holds a, b and every number between (a `Range<T>` value too); `until`, `indices()` and the `Until` type are
  removed (the diagnostics show the `a..b` form). A loop is `while`; `kira --fix-for [--typed] FILE...` rewrites a `for`
  (`--typed` asks the typer, in the project above the file, for an iterable the file does not write).
- `with` scopes calls and assignments on one value: `x: Clazz { ... } with { f(...)  field = v }` or `x with { ... }`, never
  `with x { }`. A bare `x with { }` statement on a value type is an error (assign it, `x = x with { }`, or make the type a Mutable
  class, whose `with` edits in place). `rules.with.fold` hints a run of statements on one Mutable class value;
  `kira --fix-with [--dry-run] FILE...` folds them (py-target projects only: other targets do not lower a `with`).
- Class fields: `require pub name: Type` (constructor parameter + public field).
  Construction is positional: `Point { 0, 1 }`, nested `Rect { Point { 0, 1 }, Point { 1, 0 } }`.
- Methods: `pub fx name: (args) ReturnType { ... }`. The C backend lowers
  methods to `Type_method(Type* this, ...)`.
- Modules: `module "app:main"` maps to `src/app/main.kira`. Multi-file use:
  `use "app:model"`.
- Stdlib modules are `kira:*` (`kira:stl` indexes core/tuples/collections/
  result/io/math). Magic types are ambient once the stdlib dependency loads;
  you do not write `use "kira:stl"` in app code.
- `trace(...)` prints with a newline; `print` / `println` / `eprint` / `assert`
  come from `kira:io`.

## Backend truth

- `if/else` and `while` (the only loop; `for` is refused, `kira --fix-for` rewrites it) lower today. Variants and generic
  traits are not lowered; trait inheritance and dispatch are.
- Classes are heap ARC (scope-end release). Field-embedded objects are
  borrowed; release on explicit return paths is skipped (leak, not crash).
- Container elements erase to a 64-bit `KiraSlot`: `Float32`/`Float64`
  elements are rejected, not silently reinterpreted.
- `Map.get`, `Stack.pop`, `Queue.dequeue` return `Maybe<T>`; payloads cast
  back at use sites.
- `@_opaque` / `@_extern` are the foreign edge: C symbols as written, never
  ARC'd. `build.cSources` / `build.linkFlags` carry extra C.
